    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43137" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑτερό-δοξος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>differing in opinion</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Eun.</u>
				2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>holding opinions other than the right, heterodox</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.403
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				2.9.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>BJ</u>
				2.8.5
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰατρός</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.52
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.670
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξως</span>
			<i>in heterodox manner</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς μουσικῆς ἀκροᾶσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					2.1.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
